WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.714
It's a long process and it involves your entire life.

00:00:18.714 --> 00:00:21.814
It's not like one day you're just like: 'Oh, I'm gay. Huh. Hm.'

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:29.400
I knew I was gay, like for sure gay, because I was finding stuff on the internet and I was all about it.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.500
Actually, it was a- it was a Disney movie.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.974
I remember my girlfriend and I used to practice kissing on each other.

00:00:34.974 --> 00:00:38.240
And all the girls would be like: okay we're just doing this because we're practicing now for the boys.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.000
And I'd be like: this is the best. Jackpot!

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.500
Like I was super into it.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:49.500
For me it was very much just clear that there was one main driver for my sexual energy and that was women.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:57.700
Women's bodies are great. I just - like there's literally no drive within me to like explore them on a sexual level.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:02.800
My coming out story is just kinda like: and then I met one girl and then I was like: oh f***.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.380
I just remember being eleven and twelve and all of my girl friends talking about boys they liked

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.000
and I also liked boys, but also having crushes on girls.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.000
I've never fallen in love with men. You know, and I've had boyfriends.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.000
I've never like woken up and be like: it's so good to see you and I'm so happy you're in my life.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.020
But when I have girlfriends I'm like...

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:21.900
I'm like a puppy.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.300
All the way through highschool I would say things like:

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.500
"Well there's just something about the way a guy holds you that..

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:32.500
Women are hot and they're beautiful and I love to touch them, but I wouldn't seriously date a woman.

00:01:32.575 --> 00:01:34.400
I wouldn't marry a woman.Things like that.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.380
As I've gotten older I feel like I have a deeper - I'm able to have a deeper connection with women.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.000
That's not so surface.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.820
Being gay is about being in love.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.200
It's not about sex.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.500
I don't know if I agree with that.

00:01:47.011 --> 00:01:53.500
I could see myself falling in love with a man much more easily than I could see myself having sex with a man.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:59.120
When it comes to like emotional love, beyond sex.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:02.300
Like an emotional - just like huge upheaval of everything that I know.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:08.220
I've never felt that intense of something with a girl. Nor have I longed to have that with a girl.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.500
Or met a girl that I thought I could have that with.

00:02:11.533 --> 00:02:16.333
For me being gay and my personal identity are totally different things.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:21.380
Sometimes I wear heels. Sometimes I wear combat boots. I like jazz. I love the internet.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:25.620
You know what I mean? Like that's my personal identity. That has absolutely nothing to do with being gay.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.160
I loved collecting Lisa Frank stickers. I mean like -                 I loved it.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:33.020
And I - you know to this day - like I just for some reason, man.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.880
Like these little freaking rainbows are just awesome.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:40.740
I think for my uncle he saw this as like some kind of like threat.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:47.760
But that never really like interfered with the conversation that I sort of I guess was having internally - conscious or not.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.411
About what my sexuality was.

00:02:49.411 --> 00:02:52.360
I definitely didn't want to be gay. Part of me still doesn't want to be gay.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.920
Makes life a little bit harder.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.819
I think the hardest obstacle for me has been people telling me that bisexuality isn't actually a thing.

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:02.060
Like you have to choose one or the other or you're doing it for attention.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.376
It's not true. You can like both.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:06.180
If you're struggling with your sexuality I guess the thing that I have to say is:

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.500
be comfortable and be okay just being the only person who's comfortable with your sexuality.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.500
Once you're okay with that, other people's acceptance will come.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.700
The good news is: it's getting better.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:20.300
A lot of people are gonna be there for you. Umm, and there's tons of resources out there.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:27.176
Whether you are so distraught by it or it's problematic in your life and you need the Trevor Project.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.360
A lot more people are supportive than you think.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:33.860
And if you need help there's always people on YouTube telling their story.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.840
And I'm sure you will relate to somebody on there. Just keep searching.

00:03:36.876 --> 00:03:38.316
And you're not alone.

